    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d184">

                <pb facs="0235" n="227" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg227"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/8238: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wright</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-09T14:00:00-04:00">July 9, 1938—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>54. Your letter July 7 to Briggs regarding mediation in Spain.<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d184-f1"/> You may informally advise the Secretary of State that our
                    policy of noninterference in the Spanish situation would preclude our
                    participation in any such action as that proposed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d184-f1" n="82" xml:id="d184-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; but see memorandum dated July 7, <ref target="#pg225">p.
                    225</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
